es for students to explore identity and belonging and situate their academic and career pathways within their contexts of their values and goals. Through readings, written reflections, and in-class discussions, students will develop a four-year plan, foster skills to direct their own learning, gain familiarity with Cornell's code of academic integrity, and learn strategies to balance academic success, health and wellbeing. Students also practice skills to engage responsibly with others across diverse perspectives and to be able to learn with and from their communities, both on and off campus.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: new students in Human Ecology.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Students will learn about strategies and resources to be successful in college and gain agency in navigating their academic pathways.", "Students will practice skills to communicate effectively, engage with diverse perspectives, and learn about cultural humility in preparation for community-engaged experiences."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2881, "crseId": 359823, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HE", "catalogNbr": "3100", "titleShort": "Mentoring in Higher Education", "titleLong": "Mentoring in Higher Education", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 7535, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "07:30PM", "timeEnd": "10:00PM", "startDt": "08/26/2024", "endDt": "12/09/2024", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "gwe